<h2 style="font-size: 28px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Examination Overview - NISM Series XIX-B: Alternative Investment Funds (Category III) Distributors Certification Mock Test</h2>
<br />

<p style="color: #000;">
The examination is designed to establish a common minimum knowledge benchmark for professionals engaged in the distribution of Category III Alternative Investment Funds (AIFs), including hedge funds and other leverage-based pooled investment vehicles regulated by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI).<br>

<br>This certification aims to enhance the quality, transparency, and suitability standards in the distribution of Category III AIF products by ensuring that distributors possess a clear understanding of fund structures, investment strategies, risk-return dynamics, leverage implications, taxation aspects, and regulatory guidelines governing AIFs in India. It ensures that professionals involved in marketing and distributing Category III AIF schemes are well-equipped to assess investor suitability, communicate product risks effectively, and adhere to SEBI’s compliance and disclosure requirements.<br>

<br>By strengthening conceptual clarity around alternative asset classes, fund documentation, valuation methodologies, reporting standards, and investor grievance mechanisms, the examination promotes responsible distribution practices and supports higher standards of governance and investor protection within the alternative investment ecosystem.</p>


<h2 style="font-size: 22px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Examination Objectives</h2>
<br />
<p style="color: #000;">On successful completion of the examination, the candidate should be able to:</p>
<div>

  </p>
<p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
   Understand the fundamentals of alternative asset classes and the structure, features, and regulatory positioning of Category III Alternative Investment Funds in India.
  </p>
  <p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Gain detailed knowledge of the Category III AIF ecosystem, including the roles and responsibilities of investment managers, trustees, custodians, administrators, auditors, prime brokers, and other external service providers.
  </p>
<p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Gain knowledge of taxation aspects applicable to Category III AIFs and their investors, including treatment under domestic tax laws and frameworks applicable within International Financial Services Centre (IFSC) jurisdictions.
  </p>
<p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
    Comprehend the function of Category III AIFs as sophisticated investment and risk management vehicles, including the use of leverage, derivatives, and long-short strategies.
  </p>
<p style="color: #000;">
    <img src="images/BULLET.png" alt="" style="vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 8px;" />
   Understand the concept of Net Asset Value (NAV), valuation principles applicable to listed and unlisted securities, and the role of independent third-party registered valuers in ensuring transparency and fairness.
  </p>
</div>




<h2 style="font-size: 22px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Assessment Structure</h2>
